research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json:11763:          "id": "ex-integral-of-the-floor-function-step-4-1",
research/audit/wave10-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json-11764-          "claim": "Hence $0 \\le J - 3 \\le 3/\\iota(M)$ for every $M \\ge 1$. If $J > 3$ then $(J-3)\\cdot 3^{-1} > 0$ and [L8] supplies $M \\ge 1$ with $1/\\iota(M) < (J-3)\\cdot 3^{-1}$, that is $3/\\iota(M) < J - 3$, contradicting step 3.1. So $J = 3$, that is $\\int_0^3 \\lfloor x \\rfloor\\,\\mathrm{d}x = 3$. [step 3.1, L8, L9] ∎",
